{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/105360-premade-werewolf-characters","id":105360,"title":"Premade Werewolf Characters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-03T21:21:38-07:00","id":105360,"title":"Premade Werewolf Characters","content":"Everyone needs a character sometimes, and sometimes sometimes happens at really inopportune times during a story. I am hoping to create a thread where we can make interesting characters from all aspects of werewolf ranging from any walk of life be it Pure, Forsaken, or Balehound. Characters may be niche intended for specific scenarios, to broad use in any situation. While some things may change with the eventual release of the Idigam Chronicles, these characters should have enough definition to survive the new rules when available.<br /> <br /> Template will be as follows<br /> <br /> <b>Name (human or shadow):<br /> Auspice:<br /> Aspect:<br /> Tribe:<br /> Lodge (optional):<br /> Personality:<br /> Quirk:<br /> Short Description: </b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Howls to the Rising Sun<br /> <b>Auspice:</b> Cahalith<br /> <b>Aspect:</b> Speaker<br /> <b>Tribe: </b>Storm Lord<br /> <b>Personality:</b> Howls to the Rising Sun is old, even for an Uratha approaching 120 years and she shows no signs of giving into the uppity youngsters trying to make a name for themselves. Over her long life, she has accepted the fact that the only true constant in the world are the songs that echo from one generation to the next. To this, she tracks down spirits of all kinds to find and tell their stories so that others may learn of them. In doing so, she hopes that the generations that follow will become wiser and eventually uphold in full, the duty given to them by Urfarah.<br /> <b>Quirk:</b> As to her name, she always greets the dawn with a howl that shatters the pre-dawn silence. The local populous have come to regard her howls as a local legend due to how long she has been performing it in the same area. She would be seen as more dependable then a rooster if she didn't insist of taking extended journeys into the Shadow in pursuit of her work.<br /> <b>Short Description:</b> Howls to the Rising Sun is not meant to be a wise mentor or a senile werewolf in her dotage. She is extremely sharp, and very much capable of going toe to toe with all but the strongest of Werewolves due to her many years of experience hunting in the Shadow. Instead, when she feels a story is worth telling, she requests (demands?) a gathering at the local Tur in which she sings of the stories she has gathered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}